ve/scripts/sync-public.ts","content":"  await exec(\"git remote add private ../private\", {\n    cwd: publicDir,\n    silent: true,\n  }).catch(() => {});\n  await exec(\"git fetch private --tags\", { cwd: publicDir });\n  await exec(`git fetch private v${version}`, { cwd: publicDir });\n\n  // Reset to the tag (which has the full history behind it)\n  await exec(`git reset --hard v${version}`, { cwd: publicDir });\n\n  // Remove internal files\n  for (const dir of STRIP_DIRS) {\n    const fullPath = join(publicDir, dir);\n    if (existsSync(fullPath)) {\n      await rm(fullPath, { recursive: true, force: true });\n    }\n  }\n  for (const file of STRIP_FILES) {\n    const fullPath = join(publicDir, file);\n    if (existsSync(fullPath)) {\n      await rm(fullPath, { force: true });\n    }\n  }\n  console.log(\"✓ Removed internal files\");\n\n  // Copy public files\n  const publicFilesDir = join(privateDir, \"public-release-files\");\n  if (existsSync(publicFilesDir)) {\n    await exec(`cp -r ${publicFilesDir}/. ${publicDir}/`);\n    console.log(\"✓ Copied public files\");","numLines":30,"startLine":280,"totalLines":537}},"timestamp":"2026-03-05T13:08:19.065Z"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01RtEjqjYRFEapmHGRGojUhX","type":"tool_result","content":"    28→\n    29→There is a separate public repo at `SouthBridgeAI/hankweave-runtime` which receives sanitized snapshots via the sync workflow. It publishes the public `hankweave` npm package.\n    30→\n    31→### What gets stripped before public release\n    32→\n    33→The sync process (`scripts/sync-public.ts`) removes internal-only content:\n    34→\n    35→- **Directories**: `intermediates/`, `external-docs/`, `public-release-files/`, `.github/actions/`\n    36→- **Files**: `CLAUDE.md`, `CONTRIBUTING.md`, `PUBLISHING-PLAN.md`, `telemetry.md` (root), `reference/telemetry.md` (internal version), `.github/workflows/ci.yml`, `.github/workflows/sync-public.yml`, `scripts/sync-public.ts`, `scripts/test-sync-local.ts`, `scripts/release.ts`, `.DS_Store`\n    37→\n    38→The `public-release-files/` directory contains replacements that get overlaid: a public-facing `README.md`, `LICENSE.md`, `NOTICE.md`, a sanitized `reference/telemetry.md`, and a simplified `.github/workflows/release.yml`.\n    39→\n    40→The `package.json` is transformed: name becomes `hankweave`, `publishConfig.access` becomes `public`, `homepage` points to the public repo, and `release:*` scripts are removed.\n    41→\n    42→---\n    43→\n    44→## 2. Branch Model\n    45→\n    46→```\n    47→feature branches → develop → release/alpha\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0699f0ac-31c0-43c3-bcfd-da3fdd996bc7","uuid":"e27afcc3-bdb6-46e7-b0c6-8c769bcca8f2","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/philip/projects/hw-budget-tests/plan-gen-execution/agentRoot/source/hankweave/standard-operating-procedures.md","content":"\nThere is a separate public repo at `SouthBridgeAI/hankweave-runtime` which receives sanitized snapshots via the sync workflow. It publishes the public `hankweave` npm package.\n\n### What gets stripped before public release\n\nThe sync process (`scripts/sync-public.ts`) removes internal-only content:\n\n- **Directories**: `intermediates/`, `external-docs/`, `public-release-files/`, `.github/actions/`\n- **Files**: `CLAUDE.md`, `CONTRIBUTING.md`, `PUBLISHING-PLAN.md`, `telemetry.md` (root), `reference/telemetry.md` (internal version), `.github/workflows/ci.yml`, `.github/workflows/sync-public.yml`, `scripts/sync-public.ts`, `scripts/test-sync-local.ts`, `scripts/release.ts`, `.DS_Store`\n\nThe `public-release-files/` directory contains replacements that get overlaid: a public-facing `README.md`, `LICENSE.md`, `NOTICE.md`, a sanitized `reference/telemetry.md`, and a simplified `.github/workflows/release.yml`.\n\nThe `package.json` is transformed: name becomes `hankweave`, `publishConfig.access` becomes `public`, `homepage` points to the public repo, and `release:*` scripts are removed.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Branch Model\n\n```\nfeature branches → develop → release/alpha","numLines":20,"startLine":28,"totalLines":406}},"timestamp":"2026-03-05T13:08:19.079Z"}
