{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01G6iFYUtuWjGbTraRaPvPmb","type":"tool_result","content":"   265→\n   266→From the repo root:\n   267→```bash\n   268→bun install\n   269→```\n   270→\n   271→This resolves dependencies for both workspaces, generates a new unified `bun.lock` at root, and creates a single hoisted `node_modules/` tree. The docs dependencies (`next`, `nextra`, `react`, `posthog-js`, etc.) will be added to the root lockfile but should not conflict with the runtime's dependencies -- the two packages have almost entirely different dependency trees.\n   272→\n   273→**Step 1.5: Verify docs build locally**\n   274→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0699f0ac-31c0-43c3-bcfd-da3fdd996bc7","uuid":"1d1753ee-40c2-43f0-954a-fcfd7d84055d","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/philip/projects/hw-budget-tests/plan-gen-execution/agentRoot/plan/merged/plan.md","content":"\nFrom the repo root:\n```bash\nbun install\n```\n\nThis resolves dependencies for both workspaces, generates a new unified `bun.lock` at root, and creates a single hoisted `node_modules/` tree. The docs dependencies (`next`, `nextra`, `react`, `posthog-js`, etc.) will be added to the root lockfile but should not conflict with the runtime's dependencies -- the two packages have almost entirely different dependency trees.\n\n**Step 1.5: Verify docs build locally**\n","numLines":10,"startLine":265,"totalLines":882}},"timestamp":"2026-03-05T13:11:41.951Z"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01DpZRDbvuVCKy9hau74uG4C","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01E7MsVqx63qmoBU93SodHB5","name":"Edit","input":{"replace_all":false,"file_path":"/Users/philip/projects/hw-budget-tests/plan-gen-execution/agentRoot/plan/merged/plan.md","old_string":"This resolves dependencies for both workspaces, generates a new unified `bun.lock` at root, and creates a single hoisted `node_modules/` tree. The docs dependencies (`next`, `nextra`, `react`, `posthog-js`, etc.) will be added to the root lockfile but should not conflict with the runtime's dependencies -- the two packages have almost entirely different dependency trees.","new_string":"This resolves dependencies for both workspaces, generates a new unified `bun.lock` at root, and creates a single hoisted `node_modules/` tree. The docs dependencies (`next`, `nextra`, `react`, `posthog-js`, etc.) will be added to the root lockfile but should not conflict with the runtime's dependencies — the two packages have almost entirely different dependency trees.\n\nCheck the `bun install` output for warnings. One potential friction point: the root `package.json` has `\"peerDependencies\": { \"typescript\": \"^5.9.2\" }` while the docs `package.json` has `\"devDependencies\": { \"typescript\": \"^5.0.0\" }`. Bun may emit a peer dependency mismatch warning. This is cosmetic — it does not affect the build — but if it does, the docs `typescript` range could be narrowed to `\"^5.9.2\"` to match."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":386,"cache_read_input_tokens":81317,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":386},"output_tokens":440,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0699f0ac-31c0-43c3-bcfd-da3fdd996bc7","uuid":"03c6eb77-f6