{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01WPRcDedyp8bEBqbtncu7L8","type":"tool_result","content":"    88→\n    89→## d. Conventions and Patterns\n    90→\n    91→### Observed code conventions\n    92→\n    93→1. **Scripts are TypeScript.** All build/release/sync scripts are `.ts` files run with `bun`.\n    94→2. **Relative paths from `import.meta.dir`.** Scripts use `path.join(import.meta.dir, \"..\")` to resolve project root.\n    95→3. **`Bun.spawn` for shell commands.** Scripts use `Bun.spawn([\"sh\", \"-c\", cmd])`. Note: each script defines its own `exec()` helper with different signatures. `sync-public.ts` has `exec(cmd, { cwd?, silent? })`, while `release.ts` has `exec(command, { silent?, allowFailure? })`. These are not shared. The implementing agent should not assume one script's `exec()` options exist in the other.\n    96→4. **Two-space indent, 100-char line width.** Enforced by Biome.\n    97→5. **LF line endings.** Enforced by `.gitattributes`.\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0699f0ac-31c0-43c3-bcfd-da3fdd996bc7","uuid":"8a5a0300-4b5a-4f58-a7e2-850d5a13c5be","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/philip/projects/hw-budget-tests/plan-gen-execution/agentRoot/plan/merged/plan.md","content":"\n## d. Conventions and Patterns\n\n### Observed code conventions\n\n1. **Scripts are TypeScript.** All build/release/sync scripts are `.ts` files run with `bun`.\n2. **Relative paths from `import.meta.dir`.** Scripts use `path.join(import.meta.dir, \"..\")` to resolve project root.\n3. **`Bun.spawn` for shell commands.** Scripts use `Bun.spawn([\"sh\", \"-c\", cmd])