{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01AX7Wz9m2HhepCcBzcEvaGs","type":"tool_result","content":"   395→const INTERNAL_FILES_TO_STRIP = [\n   396→  \"intermediates/\",\n   397→  \"external-docs/\",\n   398→  \"CLAUDE.md\",\n   399→  \"CONTRIBUTING.md\",\n   400→  \"standard-operating-procedures.md\",\n   401→  \"docs/\",\n   402→];\n   403→```\n   404→\n   405→This ensures the docs workspace is stripped from `release/alpha` during the release process (the `develop -> release/alpha` merge step). An important subtlety: the release script already has logic (at lines 366-385) to auto-resolve modify/delete merge conflicts on files in the `INTERNAL_FILES_TO_STRIP` list. Once `\"docs/\"` is added, any docs changes on `develop` that conflict with the stripped `release/alpha` branch will be handled automatically. This is correct behavior and requires no additional code.\n   406→\n   407→Note on the `startsWith` check: the conflict auto-resolution logic at `release.ts:380` checks `f.startsWith(s)` against entries in `INTERNAL_FILES_TO_STRIP`. Git reports file paths relative to repo root, e.g., `docs/content/guides/getting-started.mdx`. Since the strip entry is `\"docs/\"`, the `startsWith` match evaluates correctly: `\"docs/content/guides/getting-started.mdx\".startsWith(\"docs/\")` is `true`. This has been verified against the code.\n   408→\n   409→**Step 3.4: Update `scripts/release.ts` schema handling for docs**\n   410→\n   411→After migration, `generate-schemas` writes schemas to both `schemas/` (runtime) and `docs/public/schemas/` (docs site). The release script needs three fixes to account for this:\n   412→\n   413→1. **Validation phase schema diff check** (line 427): The `git diff --name-only schemas/` check that warns about schema changes only covers `schemas/`. Extend it to also check `docs/public/schemas/`:\n   414→\n   415→```typescript\n   416→const schemaChanges = await exec(\"git diff --name-only schemas/ docs/public/schemas/